WEBVTT

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:04.190
The Pokémon World Championships...

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:08.240
A trial to crown
the greatest Pokémon battler.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:13.290
In the hopes of battling Dande,
the current Supreme Monarch,

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.080
Satoshi is participating
in the Championships.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.420
Satoshi’s next opponent is...

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.590
...Dracaena of the Kalos Elite Four,
a Hyper Class competitor ranked 12th.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.970
With the help of
his former companion, Citron,

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:31.100
Satoshi trained
Negigaknight and Uonoragon...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.020
...and succeeded
in teaching them new moves.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.390
And now...

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.940
It has been many moons,
Sir Satoshi.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:45.900
Mr. Gampi!

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.490
Oh! Negigaknight!

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.700
Thy Kamonegi hath evolved?

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.660
Yup!

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.410
Good! He is lucky to have thee, Negigaknight!

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.920
Do not forget thy knightly spirit!

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:03.210
And who is this Pokémon?

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:03.960
That’s...

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:10.590
Huh?

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.350
Ms. Dracaena!

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.230
Oh my, what a simply
<i>precious</i> little Pikachu!

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.900
And you...
You must be Uonoragon.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.900
It’s <i>such</i> a pleasure to meet you!
I have heard so much about you.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:34.660
Madame Dracaena said she would be
most delighted to meet you before the battle.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.870
How do you do?

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.080
Come, now.
You greet him, as well.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.470
Quite lovely, don’t you think?

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.050
This is my most precious partner.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:55.350
We are ever-so pleased
to make your acquaintance.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.600
Yeah!
Th-The pleasure’s all mine!

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.690
I had a look at your battle record.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.020
However...

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:10.570
Your forward march ends today.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.740
And with that,
I wish you a <i>wonderful</i> day!

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.000
That really got me nervous...

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.380
What tremendous tenacity...

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.630
What did you think of them?

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.680
I do believe
I will enjoy today’s battle.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:20.120
The Pokémon World
Championships’ Hyper Class!

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.120
Today’s matchup is between
these two,

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.830
both aiming to become
the world’s greatest Pokémon Trainer!

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:31.790
Hyper Class, ranked 12th:
Competitor Dracaena of the Kalos Elite Four!

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.590
She seems pretty kind.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.600
Absolutely not!
She deceives everyone with that smile.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:45.640
You can trust my bro on that!
He didn’t stand a chance against her!

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:49.480
You didn’t have to mention that...

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.150
Her opponent, ranked 15th
and also in the Hyper Class...

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.940
...is Competitor Satoshi
from the Kanto Region!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.780
Hello!

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.740
Satoshi!

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.530
You got this!

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:05.040
This battle will be a 2v2.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:09.670
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:10.670
3!

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.670
2!

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.670
1!

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:13.630
Go!

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:16.510
Negigaknight, I choose you!

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:16.510
I’m counting on you, Onvern!

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.180
Onvern, huh?

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:30.230
Onvern! Sound Wave Pokémon!
Flying/Dragon type!

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:34.770
Flying through the darkness, it weakens enemies
with ultrasonic waves that could crush stone!

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.780
Its fangs finish the fight!

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.280
Will they be all right?

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:44.280
The Fighting-type Negigaknight is weak to
the Flying-type Onvern.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.750
Negigaknight,
keep your eyes on Onvern!

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.290
Battle, start!

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.170
Fangs of Rage!

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:56.750
Brutal Swing!

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:03.010
Oh, dear.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:07.770
It unleashes a Brutal Swing,
expertly using its shield!

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:10.390
Competitor Dracaena is astonished, too!

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.770
Very impressive.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.860
Amazing!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.900
Well done, Negigaknight!

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:19.320
He’s paying close attention to his foe.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:25.830
Okay! Great work, Negigaknight!

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:28.790
Oh, my...
I think you may be underestimating us.

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:30.830
Onvern! Blast Waves!

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:44.180
What <i>is</i> this...?!

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:59.320
You see?
No more guarding.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.820
Negigaknight!
Pick up your shield!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.370
Dragon Pulse!

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:16.880
Negigaknight!

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.250
Blast Waves!

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.480
It’s now or never,
Negigaknight!

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:39.570
Grab your sword and shield!

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.830
Good, Negigaknight!

00:07:54.500 --> 00:08:00.090
Truly indomitable!
Negigaknight reclaims its sword and shield!

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:05.340
Dragon Pulse!

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.220
Here we go, Negigaknight!
Star Assault!

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:18.850
Onvern!

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:24.690
What?!

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:27.950
Onvern’s massive wings
block the Star Assault!

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.490
Well done!

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:51.680
Oh, dear...
You <i>are</i> robust.

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:56.310
Don’t push yourself!
Come back, Negigaknight!

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:00.150
You’ll have your chance later.
Rest for now.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.690
Calling him back here
was a wise move.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:08.700
Using Star Assault
renders you immobile for a bit.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.530
Satoshi’s smart.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:11.740
So who’s his next...?

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:13.910
My heart’s pounding really fast.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.500
Negigaknight was able to damage it...

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.800
Now it’s up to you
to bring it home!

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:27.260
Uonoragon!

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.400
Competitor Satoshi’s second Pokémon
is Uonoragon!

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.990
A rare Pokémon
discovered in the Galar Region!

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.710
Oh, there you are, Uonoragon.
I have been quite eager to battle you.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.710
Fangs of Rage!

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:05.630
Here it comes!

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:06.880
Ice Fang!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.020
You okay, Uonoragon?

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.350
He’s in trouble already?!

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:25.860
Fangs of Rage is a powerful move.
It cuts the opponent’s stamina in half!

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:27.900
But look at Onvern!

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:33.160
Both sides took heavy damage!
Onvern in particular took a super effective hit!

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:34.990
Come back, Onvern!

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:40.290
Now, it’s your turn, Tyltalis!

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:46.290
There it is... Tyltalis!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.800
Competitor Dracaena’s second
is Tyltalis!

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:54.550
Tyltalis! Humming Pokémon!
Dragon/Flying type!

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:59.180
This Pokémon has a kind disposition, but if it’s provoked,
it will threaten opponents with shrill cries...

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.560
...before attacking them
without mercy!

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.250
Hey! Uonoragon!

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.370
Oh, dear... My, my...

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:26.170
Sheesh... What is it <i>thinking?!</i>

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:27.750
It’s ‘cause of how it was fluttering.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.340
Just like when it bit
Negigaknight’s sword.

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:33.380
I guess it’s just drawn
to things that sway.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:36.390
An astonishing leap into action
by Uonoragon!

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:38.100
Let’s make use of that, then!

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:39.430
Ice Fang!

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:43.100
Cotton Guard!

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:50.480
It blocked the Ice Fang!

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.990
Tyltalis’s Defense rose drastically!

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:57.450
Aren’t its plumes just lovely?

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:00.240
They can be used to
avoid heavy damage, too.

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:05.790
Both Onvern and Tyltalis are way too good
at using their wings for defense!

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.670
Yeah, that’s it!
That’s <i>exactly</i> what got you, right?

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.050
I told you,
you didn’t have to mention that...

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.470
How do you like this, then?

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:17.510
A Key Stone?!

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:21.220
Power of dragons, awaken!

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.020
Mega Evolve!

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.120
It has Mega Evolved!

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.170
Mega Tyltalis!

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:51.880
So pretty!

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:53.880
She’s finally Mega Evolved it!

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:57.260
Madame Dracaena
appears to be enjoying herself.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.970
Now, let’s do it!
God Bird!

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:09.940
Bring it on!

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:10.900
Jaw Bite!

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:16.650
Ice Fang!

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:27.540
The God Bird attack lands!

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:32.170
Figures... Its speed and power are on
a whole other level now that it’s Mega Evolved.

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:35.380
Play Rough!

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:52.060
You okay, Uonoragon?!

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:58.190
It’s so soft and fluffy,
but it’s got perfect offense <i>and</i> defense!

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.360
Its plumes...

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:04.700
That’s it!

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.200
You figured it out too, Eureka?

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.370
This brings me back...

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:14.040
Satoshi always surpasses
anything we can imagine!

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:16.340
Uonoragon! Water Gun!

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:21.010
Use God Bird again!

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:27.600
Mega Tyltalis blocks with its wings!

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:28.390
Yes!

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:29.100
What?!

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:35.900
The ferocious Water Gun
has drenched Mega Tyltalis’s prided wings!

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.030
You have <i>quite</i> the nerve!

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:39.070
Let’s finish this!

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:40.650
Dragon Dive!

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:43.530
No, Satoshi! Don’t!

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:54.710
It didn’t work?!

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:57.710
It doesn’t affect Mega Tyltalis!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.630
What’s going on?

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:03.590
Tyltalis is a Dragon/Flying type,
but when it Mega Evolves...

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.390
It becomes Dragon/Fairy.

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:09.970
You acted <i>exactly</i>
as I anticipated you would, little Satoshi.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:14.480
Dragon-type moves
don’t work on Fairy types!

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.560
Wide Breaker!

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:22.740
Ice Fang!

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:36.790
Come back, Uonoragon!

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.920
It’s all up to you,
Negigaknight!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.430
Oh, dear.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:50.060
What’s this?
Uonoragon came back out?!

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.430
What’s up?

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:57.730
You wanna cheer for Negigaknight?

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:02.480
It seems Competitor Satoshi
is letting Uonoragon watch the battle.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:07.320
I love your spirit.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.910
Allow me to answer in turn.

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:10.370
Wide Breaker!

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:14.790
Star Assault!

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:37.350
Tyltalis is unable to battle!

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.230
How is this possible?!

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:40.940
Yay!

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:44.070
Yeah! Amazing, Negigaknight!

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:48.360
Uonoragon had chipped away
at Mega Tyltalis’s stamina.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.780
But he can’t relax just yet!

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.240
Thank you, Tyltalis.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:58.540
You fought very well.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:12.600
Negigaknight is unable to battle!

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:14.310
Negigaknight!

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:20.690
What an upheaval!
Negigaknight has run out of strength!

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:24.320
Such vigor! Thou kept standing back up
for the sake of thy lord!

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:26.490
Thou art a true knight!

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:28.530
Come back, Negigaknight!

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:31.370
Thank you.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.790
Now Negigaknight, too?

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.960
It wants to cheer on Uonoragon?

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:42.630
Yes! It’s the passionate friendship
between Pokémon!

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:52.090
I see!
You wanna support Uonoragon, too!

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:55.390
Okay!

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:57.640
I’m counting on you,
Uonoragon!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.560
I see. Well, if so...

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.020
Go, Onvern!

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:11.070
You are <i>quite</i> remarkable,
to push me this far...

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.910
But that ends now!

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:14.870
We’re gonna win!

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.450
Come on, Uonoragon!

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:20.660
Dragon Pulse!

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:23.920
Dragon Dive!

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:40.140
Uonoragon!

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:44.230
Blast Waves!

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:49.360
Competitor Dracaena
keeps up the pressure!

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:54.660
Yes! Stand up!

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:02.040
Uonoragon!
It’s time to finish this!

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:06.630
Here it comes, Onvern!

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.210
Dragon Dive!

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.590
Dragon Pulse!

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:39.700
Onvern is unable to battle!
Uonoragon wins!

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.000
As such, the winner is
Competitor Satoshi!

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.830
Competitor Satoshi wins!

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:48.880
He has overcome
Competitor Dracaena of the Elite Four!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.840
Ow, ow, ow...

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:01.140
We did it, Negigaknight!

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:05.560
Oh, dear...

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:08.520
It seems we lost.
What a shame.

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.980
You gave it your all, Onvern.

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.650
Based on the results of this battle,

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:18.240
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:23.450
Competitor Satoshi climbs to
9th place, in the Hyper Class!

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:24.960
9th?!

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:26.790
You did it!

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:28.210
He’s made it all the way to 9th!

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:30.960
Amazing, Satoshi!

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:33.210
Congratulations!

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:41.760
Satoshi. Congratulations on climbing
to 9th place, the top of the Hyper Class.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.470
Thank you very much!

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:47.480
The battles to come
will not be quite so easy.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:49.980
I know! I’ll give it my all!

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:55.110
Your Negigaknight and Uonoragon
are <i>entirely</i> too charming.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:57.820
I’ll be cheering you on.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.820
Continue striving for thy goal.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:01.320
I will, Mr. Gampi!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.830
What is it, Eureka?

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:08.670
I’ve decided!

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:12.790
Ms. Dracaena!
Marry my brother, s’il-vous-plaît!

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:18.930
You’re just so strong
and responsible...

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:22.260
I can’t think of any other person
fit to marry him!

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.970
Oh, dear...
What ever am I to do?

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.770
Wha—? How come?!

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:31.310
Don’t “How come?!” me!

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:36.820
Satoshi has defeated Dracaena of the
Kalos Elite Four and risen even further in the ranks.

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:42.530
Soon, he will be able to challenge
those eight world-class trainers, the Masters Eight!

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:09.490
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:10.790
Go!

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:15.460
Lutia’s... Miraculous...
Contest Scouting!

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:19.250
This is the trainer
I’m gonna scout today!

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:21.090
Huh? Scout?!

00:23:21.090 --> 00:23:23.170
Koharu, you’re gonna
participate in a Contest?!

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.550
Um... I’m still not entirely sure.

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:28.010
Well, we’ll be at the venue,
in either case!

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:29.470
See ya!

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:31.180
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:34.350
Eevee and Nymphia!
A Meeting and a Reunion!!
